{
  "id": "COMPOUND:32188 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine may exert its biological effects through multiple distinct pathways targeting different molecular entities that ultimately lead to the inhibition of SMMC-7721. The first pathway involves the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is a known target of WS-5995 B, a compound that in turn targets SMMC-7721. The second pathway involves the dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinase, which is also a target of Javanicoside F, another compound that acts on SMMC-7721. The third pathway involves a more complex molecular entity that, upon targeting, also leads to the inhibition of SMMC-7721. These findings collectively suggest that 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine may act through multiple mechanisms, potentially involving protein kinases and proteasome components, to exert a cytotoxic effect on SMMC-7721. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for 6-Acetonyldihydrochelerythrine to modulate cellular processes in SMMC-7721 through diverse molecular targets, supporting a mechanism of action that is both complex and biologically relevant.",
